Goal:

Deploy an AI-powered Log Analyzer that:

Runs inside a GCP VM or Cloud Shell

Uses Vertex AI Gemini 2.5 Flash

Automatically performs Root Cause Analysis (RCA) on logs

 1. VM / Environment Setup
Step 1.1 — Launch Cloud Shell or GCE VM

Use either:

gcloud compute ssh ai-log-analyzer --zone=us-central1-a


or open Cloud Shell from your GCP Console.

Step 1.2 — Update and install required packages
sudo apt update -y
sudo apt install -y python3 python3-pip git

Step 1.3 — Install required Python libraries
pip install --upgrade google-auth google-auth-httplib2 google-auth-oauthlib requests


These are the minimal dependencies to authenticate and call Vertex AI’s REST API.

 2. Enable Required GCP Services

Ensure your GCP project has the following APIs enabled:

gcloud services enable aiplatform.googleapis.com
gcloud services enable generativelanguage.googleapis.com
gcloud services enable logging.googleapis.com


Check status:

gcloud services list --enabled | grep ai

 3. Configure Permissions

Make sure your VM’s service account has these roles:

roles/aiplatform.user
roles/aiplatform.serviceAgent
roles/storage.admin
roles/logging.viewer
roles/logging.logWriter


Check:

gcloud projects get-iam-policy testadi-459816 | grep aiplatform

 4. Verify Available Models

To list all available Gemini models in your project:

python3 - <<'EOF'
import requests, os, json
from google.auth import default
from google.auth.transport.requests import Request

creds, _ = default(scopes=["https://www.googleapis.com/auth/cloud-platform"])
creds.refresh(Request())
token = creds.token
endpoint = "https://us-central1-aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1/projects/testadi-459816/locations/us-central1/publishers/google/models"
resp = requests.get(endpoint, headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {token}"})
print(resp.status_code, json.dumps(resp.json(), indent=2))
EOF


 You should see models like:

models/gemini-2.5-flash
models/gemini-2.5-pro
models/gemini-2.5-flash-lite

 5. Create AI Analyzer Script

Create the file:

vi ai_analyzer_vertexai.py

6. Run the Analyzer
python3 ai_analyzer_vertexai.py


 Expected Output:

AI Root-Cause Analysis Result:

Incident Summary: High CPU utilization in Service X
Root Cause: Memory leak or inefficient loop
Impacted Component: Compute instance
Evidence: CPU 98% → auto-restart triggered
Recommended Fixes:
1. Optimize code
2. Implement autoscaling
3. Add alerting

